The key changes in `unittests/class_inheritance.chai`:

```chaiscript
// Typed function - parameter declared as Base
def call_do_something(Base obj) {
  return obj.do_something()
}

assert_equal(20, call_do_something(Base()))     // Base works
assert_equal(20, call_do_something(Derived()))  // Derived accepted, calls base method
assert_equal(500, call_do_something(Derived2())) // Derived2 accepted, calls its override

// Typed attribute accessor
def get_x(Base obj) {
  return obj.x
}

// Multi-level: GrandChild passed to Base-typed function
assert_equal(2, call_do_something(gc))
assert_equal(1, get_x(gc))

// Mid-level typed function
def call_do_other(Derived obj) {
  return obj.do_other()
}
assert_equal(6, call_do_other(GrandChild()))
```

This all works correctly because `Param_Types::match()` in `proxy_functions.hpp:123` already uses `Dynamic_Object::type_matches()` to walk the inheritance chain, so a `Derived` object matches a `Base`-typed parameter. Polymorphic dispatch also works — `Derived2`'s override of `do_something()` is called even when passed through `call_do_something(Base obj)`.

All 296 tests pass.
